INSERT INTO feature VALUES('spheres','identity','The 2-sphere and the 3-sphere as presentations','presented-circle','partial','notable',NULL,'A cell at the reflexivity of a point, `surf : Path.here Base2 <-> Path.here Base2`, presents the 2-sphere, and a cell one reflexivity higher the 3-sphere. The path type at the wrapped point is the words over the cell, in the checker and in the kernel. Those words are abelian: their letters sort by cell and count, a letter cancels its inverse at any distance, and two words that differ by a count stay apart. A case over a sphere takes an arm at its cell, and `Path.ap` of the case on the cell reduces to that arm, one layer per reflexivity between the cell''s type and the map''s domain. A dependent case into a path family omits its arm at the cell: each engine reads a transport along the bound path as an endpoint, and its image of the cell is the conjugation of the family''s endpoint images, reduced at reflexivity. A case into the universe takes `ua` of a homotopy of the identity at the 2-cell, the universe family at a cell: transport along that cell applies the homotopy at the point, and `ua` of the identity equivalence is reflexivity. An answer at the point that holds a letter moves to itself where both images of the cell are empty, read by one syntactic rule in each engine, and waits elsewhere. The degree of a map of the 3-sphere that fixes the point by its cases is the winding of its image of the 3-cell, a case over the words at the 3-cell whose `here` arm reads its words from the stated type; the identity''s degree is one, by conversion. The degree of a pointed map carries its image of the 3-cell along its pointing: `Path.ap` of a bound map reads its domain from the binder''s arrow, and the kernel checks each layer of the tower against the cell.','surface-lowering core-term core-nbe core-checker kernel-core kernel-term','corpus/model/identity/sphere.gandr corpus/model/identity/sphere-words.gandr corpus/model/identity/sphere-maps.gandr corpus/model/identity/degree.gandr corpus/pathological/identity/sphere-maps.gandr corpus/model/identity/sphere-whiskers.gandr corpus/model/identity/hopf.gandr corpus/ledger/features/spheres.gandr','corpus/ledger/features/spheres.gandr','#6773');
